<title>JAPAN: Japan May construction orders up 6.2 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan May construction orders up 6.2 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Orders received by 50 major Japanese construction companies in May rose 6.2 percent from a year earlier to 1.27 trillion yen, the Construction Ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>In April, orders fell 16.1 percent year-on-year to 1.00 trillion yen.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of overall construction orders in May (in yen, with year-ago percentage comparisons, all figures rounded):</p>
<p>   Domestic private-sector orders    868.97 bln (+15.4 pct)</p>
<p>   Domestic public sector orders     265.76 bln (-12.4 pct)</p>
<p>Orders for foreign government facilities in Japan and orders</p>
<p>worth less than 10 mln yen		37.99 bln ( -8.5 pct)</p>
<p>   Orders received abroad		 99.85 bln ( -0.6 pct)</p>
</text>
